From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:18:48 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: move AP/STA kernel-doc to its function

The AP/STA virtual interface creation comment precedes an AWDL cleanup
helper instead of brcmf_apsta_add_vif(). W=1 reports a mismatched function
name and an undocumented cfg parameter when compiling cfg80211.c.

Move the existing comment immediately above the function it describes so
the brcm80211 W=1 verification can run without kernel-doc warnings.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit b53f0bb8e8d9d3ec827f1438b6055c02fa091919)
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c    | 20 +++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index d285183869..3d464e371c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -595,16 +595,6 @@ brcmf_cfg80211_update_proto_addr_mode(struct wireless_dev *wdev)
 						ADDR_INDIRECT);
 }
 
-/**
- * brcmf_apsta_add_vif() - create a new AP or STA virtual interface
- *
- * @wiphy: wiphy device of new interface.
- * @name: name of the new interface.
- * @params: contains mac address for AP or STA device.
- * @type: interface type.
- *
- * Return: pointer to new vif on success, ERR_PTR(-errno) if not
- */
 static void brcmf_awdl_cleanup_locked(struct brcmf_cfg80211_info *cfg)
 {
 	struct brcmf_cfg80211_vif *vif;
@@ -866,6 +856,16 @@ int brcmf_awdl_del_vif(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev)
 	return err;
 }
 
+/**
+ * brcmf_apsta_add_vif() - create a new AP or STA virtual interface
+ *
+ * @wiphy: wiphy device of new interface.
+ * @name: name of the new interface.
+ * @params: contains mac address for AP or STA device.
+ * @type: interface type.
+ *
+ * Return: pointer to new vif on success, ERR_PTR(-errno) if not
+ */
 static
 struct wireless_dev *brcmf_apsta_add_vif(struct wiphy *wiphy, const char *name,
 					 struct vif_params *params,
